// @test: returning a Vec field of a by-value struct parameter is an independent owner (#412)
// @description: the callee deep-copies a by-value struct parameter, but its scope-exit
//   reclaim freed that copy's owned fields even when one of them was the value being
//   returned -- so the caller's new binding and the callee's copy held the same heap
//   buffer and the process aborted with "free(): double free detected in tcache 2"
//   (exit 134) after having produced correct output. A member-access return now
//   deep-copies the returned Vec, so the returned value owns its buffer and the base
//   binding is cleaned up normally. Found by VybForge; see issue #412.
// @category: ownership, vec, struct
// @expect-output: w=5
// @expect-return: 0

share(all)
struct Big {
    a<Vec<Int>>,
    b<Int>
}

share(all)
f(b<Big>)<Vec<Int>> -> {
    return b.a
}

main()<Int> -> {
    v<Vec<Int>> = Vec()
    for (i in 0..4) { v.push(i) }
    x<Big> = Big { a = v, b = 1 }
    w<Vec<Int>> = f(x)
    println("w=" + w.len().to_string())
    return 0
}
